T-004 acceptance re-run, both runtimes, captured 2026-08-25 against the current tree, after
this session's cross-model-panel remediation of three sh/ps1 twin divergences the anthropic
slot recorded:
  (a) the named-SKIP dependency list rendered with a TRAILING SPACE in Bash ('(Epic A4 )')
      and without one in PowerShell ('(Epic A4)'). Cause: 'sed s/+$/ /', a typo for
      's/+$//'. Fixed, and the emitted shape is now asserted in BOTH twins, so the
      divergence cannot silently return.
  (b) the Bash anchor-fingerprint extractor used a greedy '.\*sha256:' and took the LAST
      digest in the sed span while the PowerShell twin's lazy match took the FIRST. They
      agreed only because the span currently holds exactly one. Bash now takes the first.
  (c) 'sed -n ...p | head -1' under 'set -o pipefail' coupled schema_from_design's status to
      SIGPIPE. Replaced with a pipe-free awk. Measured: the hazard needs sed output to exceed
      the pipe buffer, so the two-match case the finding names would NOT have tripped it;
      the class is removed anyway.

Both twins now emit byte-identical SKIP lines (verified by cmp) and both report 44/0.
The suite's own 116-case mutation proof (mutation-proof.sh) was re-run against the modified
suite: 116 killed, 0 survived.

